  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: bfcb709b487afd749b8fbd2c4c50e261, type: 3}
  m_Name: Warlock
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Key: Warlock
  Label: Warlock
  Blurb: Has found that the shortest route to power runs straight through himself.
  Vision:
    Fantasy: "Dark-caster type of hero. Somewhat evil, and looks for opportunities
      to gain power at the cost of others.\t"
    Role: Blood-magic caster. can sacrifice HP to cast, should have a kit that allows
      draining health from enemies and spending his own health for certain skills.
      He is best played mixing branches together.
    SignatureMechanic: 'Blood magic: pays with his own health for stronger attacks.
      Does not need to be exclusive to him.'
    UltraStyle: Demonology
    Ultras:
    - Name: Demon Form
      Effect: Transform the Warlock into a powerful demon, with signature attacks.
        Health/maxhealth increases by X%, but current health stays the same relatively
        (so if warlock had 50% total health before transform he will also have it
        after, and viceversa when transforming back, attack becomes a melee attack
        that deals shadow damage. Has s special Chaos bolt (similar artwork to blood
        bolt, but deals shadow damage). Lasts 3 turns
      Unlock: It is on the Trunk, but requires a special material that is only found
        later in the game
    Branches:
    - GridBranch: a
      Becomes: Blood magic user, sacrifice health for damage.
      IntendedKit: Blood bolt => Life Tap (health for an ability charge, WoW-style)
        => ?
      Summon: '?'
    - GridBranch: b
      Becomes: Self-heal focussed
      IntendedKit: Drain life => ?
      Summon: '?'
    - GridBranch: c
      Becomes: Demon summoner
      IntendedKit: Summon imp => Summon succubus => Summon ??
      Summon: Summon demon army (replacemenet summon, but instead of 1 it summons
        multiple demons)
    Overlaps: Tinkerer is the other Intelligence caster - to settle once the Tinkerer
      is redefined.
    OpenQuestions: "Felguards and bigger troops for the Demon Army - deferred until
      the grid has room, and material-gated when they come (no early spike). Rain
      of Fire and Soul Harvest are first-draft Demonology Ultras (Claude, 2026-10-04)
      - keep, change or replace? Balance: every Warlock number is a first draft (see
      docs/BALANCING.md \xA75aa). The sacrifice-a-party-member Ultra moved to the
      Cultist (2026-10-04)."
